00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:38.250
We'll be taking a deep dive into 'Palm Springs' explaining its time loops and what exactly happened in that ending

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:44.219
But, before we get stuck in an infinite time loop, make sure to LIKE and Subscribe for more breakdowns, theories, and deep dives

00:00:44.289 --> 00:00:49.769
Palm Springs is the story of Niles, a man forced to live the same day over and over again

00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:58.589
Unlike movies like Groundhog Day which take time for the protagonist to get into their loop 'Palm Springs'

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:03.000
focuses on Niles who has already lived this day hundreds if not thousands of times

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.769
He's complacent, thinks life is meaningless and has given in that, this is his fate

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:12.210
"The only way to really live in this is to embrace the fact that nothing matters"

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.560
"I think your best bet is just to learn how to suffer existence"

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:23.460
Niles has to relive the wedding of his girlfriend's best friend's wedding over and over, a wedding which takes place November 9th

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:30.960
which coincidentally is the same day Albert Einstein received the Nobel Prize for his work on Theoretical Physics. For Niles

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.610
this is a day like any other.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:38.099
He's completely memorized where everyone on the dance floor will be to try to woo Sarah, the bride's sister

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:44.909
and Sarah like Niles is extremely flawed. She believes love doesn't exist in that marriage is bullshit

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:48.269
"Nobody can stand the idea of being alone"

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:51.630
"So we

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.899
buy into this pageantry, celebrates it's...

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:56.560
bullshit

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:02.640
So, it makes sense that the man who thinks life is meaningless and the woman who believes love doesn't exist to get stuck in a

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:08.819
time loop together for all eternity. You see the night they're about to get it on, Niles is attacked by a man

00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:12.509
we'll come to know as Roy, Roy is also stuck in the loop

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:19.190
In fact, it was Niles who brought Roy to the mysterious time-loop cave one night during a coke induced bender

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:23.629
Oh, yeah, there's this cave that has a portal in it that traps people in the time loop

00:02:23.629 --> 00:02:26.869
The problem is there doesn't seem to be a way to end the loop

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:30.050
If you go into the portal you just wake up and start the day over again

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:33.709
But if you don't go into it, you'll wake up and start the day over anyway

00:02:33.709 --> 00:02:40.759
There's no escape. Roy holds Niles responsible for getting trapped in this loop and often comes looking for him to torture

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.090
He believes marriage is a bottomless pit, but as we'll find out later

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:51.520
He lets go of his hatred towards Niles and embraces his life. Hopefully, Niles can learn that he can change too

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.840
"What happened to marriage being a bottomless pit of sorrow?"

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.760
"Things change you know..."

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.480
"Priorities change"

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:05.600
Over the course of the film, Niles and Sarah fall in love, go on adventures and just have fun with the card they have been dealt

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:12.340
We learned that Sarah had sex with her sister's fiance the day before the wedding. That pain of the terrible things

00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:15.949
she's done eats away at her and she takes it out on Niles. In retaliation,

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:21.500
he tells her he had sex with her multiple times in previous loops before she got stuck

00:03:21.569 --> 00:03:24.319
This is the classic romantic comedy structure

00:03:24.319 --> 00:03:25.109
we're about

00:03:25.109 --> 00:03:30.769
three-quarters of the way through the movie shit hits the fan and it looks like our couple might not make it through at all. Niles

00:03:30.769 --> 00:03:36.709
wakes up after their fight and for weeks? months? years? We actually don't know how long because the loop keeps repeating

00:03:36.709 --> 00:03:38.299
He can't find Sarah

00:03:38.299 --> 00:03:44.479
She's gone on her own adventure to find a way to break the loop, spending most of her time reading about Quantum Physics

00:03:45.239 --> 00:03:52.518
Eventually, she finds out that the loop has a brief 3.2-second window where one can propel themselves out using explosives, of course

00:03:52.519 --> 00:03:58.219
And she knows this could work since she experiments on a goat who the next day is no longer in her loop

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:01.429
It didn't reappear. So, it must have gone someplace else

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:05.400
Sara tells Niles the good news, but he doesn't want to leave.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.580
"Don't want to leave. There's a difference"

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.820
Oh, yeah, what's the difference?"

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.440
"I want to stay with you"

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.720
She wants to go.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:12.720
He wants to stay

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:18.940
And, Ultimately, she decides to go without him, spending her final night giving a heartfelt speech to her sister at her wedding

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:24.100
But, there's one scene that really confused me and I'm wondering if any of you who watched it caught it.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:26.240
Get ready to put on your tinfoil hat

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.560
After Sarah gives her speech

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:33.760
grandmother comes up to her and tells her how great it was. But, watch this and pay close attention to Sarah's reaction

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:36.800
"Well, I suppose now that you'll be going soon"

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:37.960
[silence]

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.960
"Good luck".

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.820
[silence]

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:48.680
I suppose now that you'll be going soon. How does Nana know here that she's leaving tonight? Is she referring to her leaving the party?

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.360
I know this is gonna sound bonkers

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:54.889
but, it almost made me think that Nana is part of the loop too, after all in this loop

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:59.479
she gets to live over and over again with the ones she loves. If she were to go back

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:03.710
Well, she's old and who knows how much time she has left.  Am I crazy?

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:05.810
Let me know what you think in the comments below

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:12.620
At the same time, Niles is moping at the bar lamenting losing the love of his life when he's given some great advice from Darla

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:15.020
"Whatever you're after, it ain't here".

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:17.500
He rushes to Sarah and professes his love

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:19.220
"I'd rather die with you"

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:21.740
"than live in this world without you"

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:26.180
Niles has gone from thinking life is meaningless to thinking life is meaningless without

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:31.980
her. Sarah has gone from believing love as a fairy tale to knowing that true love can exist

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:33.960
"In case I don't see you again..."

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:36.320
"...I love you too"

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:41.480
They head into the portal and detonate the explosives when we next find them floating in a pool together

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:45.960
and there's a brief moment of wondering whether or not their plan worked. Niles says

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:51.509
he should go pick up his dog now considering the plan did indeed work as the owners of the home they've crashed arrived

00:05:51.509 --> 00:05:56.068
It's November 10th and the day has gone forward and they've successfully broken from the loop

00:05:56.069 --> 00:05:59.878
but, more importantly, they've broken their preconceived notions of love and

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:07.420
existence. Through their love, they've realized life is worth living. The camera pants upward to reveal in the distance a pack of brontosauruses

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:08.400
Brontosauri?

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:11.320
A nod back to the night they were high on mushrooms

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:17.460
I imagine some people may interpret this as them still in some weird alternate reality, but I personally wouldn't go that far

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:23.849
It's just a fun way to end the movie. However, there is one final scene shortly after the credits, which lets us know

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:24.840
What happened to Roy?

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:26.250
He is still in the loop

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:31.229
And, at the wedding goes to Niles telling him that Sarah's theory about getting out of the loop is crazy

00:06:31.229 --> 00:06:35.038
But, it just might work Niles. However, has no idea who he is

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:40.900
Thereby letting Roy know that Sarah's plan worked and that he and Sarah made it out of the loop.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.000
Overall, I gotta say I

00:06:42.009 --> 00:06:49.318
enjoyed 'Palm Springs'.  Andy Samberg and Cristin Milioti have great chemistry, and it was a fun twist on a gimmick that has been overdone

